      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "A right triangle has legs of length $2\\,\\text{cm}$ and $4\\,\\text{cm}.$ Calculate the length of its hypotenuse.",
      "worked_solution": "Let $a=2\\,cm,$ $b=4\\,cm,$ and $c$ be the length of the hypotenuse. According to the Pythagorean theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}^{2} & ={a}^{2}+{b}^{2} \\\\ c & =\\sqrt{{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting in the values for $a$ and $b$ gives us\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\sqrt{(2)^{2}+(4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{20} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}\\,cm.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
